From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:45:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe-4-1: program RDI frame geometry

In frame based mode (RDI) the write master buffer configuration
(WR_BUFFER_CFG: words per line, height, burst length) was never written.
The vendor msm_vfe40_axi_cfg_wm_reg() programs it for frame based write
masters too. On MSM8953 RDI frames tear or get cut without it.

Add an optional wm_frame_size operation and implement it for VFE 4.1,
limited to MSM8953 (and SDM450): the vendor uses a different burst length
on MSM8916 and MSM8939, which are left unchanged.

The height field is 12 bits wide. Limit the MSM8953 RDI sink pad and
video node formats to 4096 lines and report that limit in
enum_framesizes, so link validation rejects a taller input.
vfe_enable_output() rejects an invalid height as a final safeguard.
Apply the height limit only to RDI, retaining Linux 7.3's separate PIX
and RDI stride alignment.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/55efe142d878ea2969a49e54e5017ca191d0f9f7
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
---
